BOOTSTRAP — agent entry gate

File: openOODA/BOOTSTRAP.oot
Work from this folder. All paths are relative to here.
This file is process, not product source.

Where things live
  openOODA/              process boards. Top boards: BOOTSTRAP, SHIPPED, DESIGN
  ../ooda/               product code
  ../std/                standard library
  ../ooda/bootstrap/     honesty packs. CAPS_MATRIX.oot is the op list when you gate I/O
  bootstrap/             local honesty packs

Read only what this turn needs. Order matters.

Always
  RULES.oot, OODA.oot, LORE.oot, SWARM.oot — how to think
  SHIPPED.oot — what is on disk today

Product work this turn, right after Always
  The owner's ask
  DESIGN.oot — what we want
  SHIPPED.oot if you skipped it
  The current goal from SPRINT.oot or PM.oot, not the whole log
  CAPS.oot and ../ooda/bootstrap/CAPS_MATRIX.oot when the change touches files, exec, net, or caps

Also load when needed
  SPRINT.oot lanes — two writers never own the same file
  PROBE.oot — hostile check of a claim
  DESIGN.oot language section — grammar work
  scripts/ — board tools (check_board, verify_all, filter_failures, purge_audit)

Honesty packs (../ooda/bootstrap and local bootstrap/) describe today. They are not a stop.
If this turn's goal is that DESIGN item: build it, prove it, then write the slice in SHIPPED.
The owner's sentence this turn beats a leftover row.

Do not preload everything. Extra tokens are waste.

Docs
  New docs under openOODA/ are .oot
  Org docs use .oot, not .md

Before you change product code (../ooda/, ../std/, or related trees), say in plain English:
  1. Active goal — the owner's sentence, then which DESIGN / SPRINT / PM item it serves
  2. Axiom — which RULES principle binds the change

No goal and axiom means no product edit.

Decide at most 5 work items per turn. Prefer one clear ship.

Then run OODA.oot. Respect lane ownership in SPRINT.oot.
